hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1091.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1091.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1092.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1092.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1093.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father said about the word of Allah
1093.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father said about the word of Allah
1094.1,Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah
1094.2,Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah
1095.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
1095.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
1096.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah were marrying off their daughters and they did not consult them. Malik said
1096.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah were marrying off their daughters and they did not consult them. Malik said
1097.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said about the virgin given by her father in marriage without her permission
1097.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said about the virgin given by her father in marriage without her permission
1098.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah
1098.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah
1099.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
1099.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
1100.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Ubaydullah ibn Umar whose mother was the daughter of Zayd ibn al- Khattab
1100.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Ubaydullah ibn Umar whose mother was the daughter of Zayd ibn al- Khattab
1101.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz during his khalifate
1101.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz during his khalifate
1102.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab decided about the woman who was married by a man and the marriage had been consummated
1102.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab decided about the woman who was married by a man and the marriage had been consummated
1103.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Zayd ibn Thabit said
1103.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Zayd ibn Thabit said
1104.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1104.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1105.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar- Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi from his father that when the Messenger of Allah
1105.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar- Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi from his father that when the Messenger of Allah
1106.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said
1106.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said
1107.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who made a stipulation on her husband not to take her away from her town. Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1107.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who made a stipulation on her husband not to take her away from her town. Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1108.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Miswar ibn Rifaa al- Quradhi from az-Zubayr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn az-Zubayr that Rifaa ibn Simwal divorced his wife
1108.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Miswar ibn Rifaa al- Quradhi from az-Zubayr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn az-Zubayr that Rifaa ibn Simwal divorced his wife
1109.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha
1109.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha
1110.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when asked whether it was permissible for a man to return to his wife if he had divorced her irrevocably and then another man had married her after him and died before consummating the marriage
1110.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when asked whether it was permissible for a man to return to his wife if he had divorced her irrevocably and then another man had married her after him and died before consummating the marriage
1111.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1111.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1112.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1112.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1113,"[1113] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: chaste women are First wives, and this is due to the fact that God Almighty forbids adultery."
1114.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from more than one source that when Abdullah ibn Masud was in Kufa
1114.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from more than one source that when Abdullah ibn Masud was in Kufa
1115.1,Malik said that a man who had committed fornication with a woman and the hadd-punishment had been applied to him for it
1115.2,Malik said that a man who had committed fornication with a woman and the hadd-punishment had been applied to him for it
1116.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Abd ar-Rahman and Mujamma the sons of Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Khansa bint Khidam al-Ansariya that her father gave her in marriage and she had been previously married. She disapproved of that
1116.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Abd ar-Rahman and Mujamma the sons of Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Khansa bint Khidam al-Ansariya that her father gave her in marriage and she had been previously married. She disapproved of that
1117.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that a case was brought to Umar about a marriage which had only been witnessed by one man and one woman . He said
1117.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that a case was brought to Umar about a marriage which had only been witnessed by one man and one woman . He said
1118.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Tulayha al-Asadiya was the wife of Rushayd ath-Thaqafi. He divorced her
1118.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Tulayha al-Asadiya was the wife of Rushayd ath-Thaqafi. He divorced her
1119.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar were asked about a man who had a free woman as a wife and then wanted to marry a slave-girl. They disapproved that he should combine the two of them
1119.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar were asked about a man who had a free woman as a wife and then wanted to marry a slave-girl. They disapproved that he should combine the two of them
1120.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1120.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1121.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Abd ar- Rahman that Zayd ibn Thabit said that if a man divorced his slave-girl three times and then bought her
1121.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Abd ar- Rahman that Zayd ibn Thabit said that if a man divorced his slave-girl three times and then bought her
1122.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked whether
1122.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked whether
1123.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife
1123.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife
1124.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from his father that Umar ibn al- Khattab was asked about a woman and her daughter who were in the possession of the right hand
1124.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from his father that Umar ibn al- Khattab was asked about a woman and her daughter who were in the possession of the right hand
1125.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb that a man asked Uthman ibn Affan whether one could have intercourse with two sisters who one owned. Uthman said
1125.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb that a man asked Uthman ibn Affan whether one could have intercourse with two sisters who one owned. Uthman said
1126.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said the like of that. Malik said that if a man had sexual relations with a female slave that he owned
1126.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said the like of that. Malik said that if a man had sexual relations with a female slave that he owned
1127.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave his son a slave-girl and said
1127.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave his son a slave-girl and said
1128.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that Abd arRahman ibn al-Mujabbir said that Salim ibn Abdullah gave his son a slave-girl and said
1128.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that Abd arRahman ibn al-Mujabbir said that Salim ibn Abdullah gave his son a slave-girl and said
1129.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Abu Nahshal ibn al-Aswad said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad
1129.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Abu Nahshal ibn al-Aswad said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad
1130.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he gave a slave-girl to a friend of his
1130.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he gave a slave-girl to a friend of his
1131.1,
1131.2,
1132.1,
1132.2,"Yahya narrated to me from Malik, that it reached him that a man said to Abdillah ibn Abbas: \I have divorced my wife one hundred divorces.\"" He asked"," \""What do you think is incumbent upon me?\"" Ibn Abbas said to him: \""She is divorced from you by three"," and the remaining ninety-seven you have taken the signs of Allah in jest.\"""""
1133.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Uthman ibn
Ishaq ibn Kharasha that Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb said, ""A grandmother came
to Abu Bakr as-Siddiq and asked him for her inheritance. Abu Bakr said
to her, 'You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I do not know that
you have anything in the sunna of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah
bless him and grant him peace. Go away therefore, until I have
questioned the people.' (i.e.the Companions). He questioned the
people, and al-Mughira ibn Shuba said, 'I was present with the
Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he
gave the grandmother a sixth.' Abu Bakr said, 'Was there anybody else
with you?' Muhammad ibn Maslama al-Ansari stood up and said the like
of what al-Mughira said. Abu Bakr as-Siddiq gave it to her. Then the
other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and asked him for her
inheritance. He said to her, ""You have nothing in the Book of Allah,
and what has been decided is only for other than you, and I am not one
to add to the fixed shares, other than that sixth. If there are two of
you together, it is between you. If eitherof you is left alone with
it, it is hers."""
1133.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abdullah and Hasan
1134.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Khawla ibn Hakim came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said
1134.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Khawla ibn Hakim came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said
1135.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Rabia ibn Abd ar- Rahman say that a slave could marry four women. Malik said
1135.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Rabia ibn Abd ar- Rahman say that a slave could marry four women. Malik said
1136.1,Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he had heard that in the time of the Messenger of Allah
1136.2,Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he had heard that in the time of the Messenger of Allah
1137.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn
Muhammad ibn Amribn Hazm that Abdar-Rahman ibn Hanthala az-Zurqi was
informed by a mawla of Quraysh,who used to be known as Ibn Mursi, that
he was sitting with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and when they had prayed
dhuhr, he said, ""Yarfa! Bring that letter! (a letter which he had
written about the paternal aunt.) We asked about her and asked for
information about her."" Yarfa brought it to him. He called for a small
vessel or a drinking-bowl in which there was water. He erased the
letter in it. Then he said, ""Had Allah approved of you as an heir, we
would have confirmed you. Had Allah approved of you, we would have
confirmed you."""
1137.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said
1138.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham who was the wife of Ikrima ibn Abi Jahl became muslim on the day of the conquest of Makka
1138.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham who was the wife of Ikrima ibn Abi Jahl became muslim on the day of the conquest of Makka
1139.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf came to the Messenger of Allah
1139.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf came to the Messenger of Allah
1140.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said
1140.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said
1141.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1141.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1142.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibr. Shihab from al-Araj that Abu Hurayra said
1142.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibr. Shihab from al-Araj that Abu Hurayra said
1143.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha heard Anas ibn Malik say that a certain tailor invited the Messenger of Allah
1143.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha heard Anas ibn Malik say that a certain tailor invited the Messenger of Allah
1144.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that the Messenger of Allah
1144.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that the Messenger of Allah
1145.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that somebody asked a man for his sister in marriage and the man mentioned that she had committed fornication. Umar ibn al-Khattab heard about it and he beat the man or almost beat him
1145.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that somebody asked a man for his sister in marriage and the man mentioned that she had committed fornication. Umar ibn al-Khattab heard about it and he beat the man or almost beat him
1146.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that a man who had four wives and then divorced one of them irrevocably
1146.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that a man who had four wives and then divorced one of them irrevocably
1147.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Urwa ibn az-Zubayr gave the same judgement to al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik in the year of his arrival in Madina except that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that he divorced his wife on various occasions. (i.e. not at one time)
1147.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abd ar-Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Urwa ibn az-Zubayr gave the same judgement to al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik in the year of his arrival in Madina except that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that he divorced his wife on various occasions. (i.e. not at one time)
1148,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1149,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Rafi ibn Khadij married the daughter of Muhammad ibn Maslama al-Ansari. She was with him until she grew older
